10. MR. KHALID MAQBOOL SlODlQUl, Minister for Federal Education and ProfessionalTraining, to introduce a Bill further to amend the Pakistan Study Centers Act, 1976 [ThePakistan Study Centers (Amendment) Bill, 20261.
LEGISLATIVE BUSINESS11. SENATOR MUHAMMAD AURANGZEB, Minister for Finance and Revenue, to move thatthe Bill further to amend the lncome Tax Ordinance, 2001 [The lncome Tax (ThirdAmendment) Bill, 20251, as reported by the Standing Committee, be taken into considerationat once.
L2. SENATOR MUHAMMAD AURANGZEB, Minister for Finance and Revenue, to move thatthe Bill further to amend the lncome Tax Ordinance, 2001 [The lncome Tax (Third Amendment)Bill, 20251, be passed.MOTION OF THANKS
13. Further discussion on the following motion moved by DR. TARIQ FAZAT CHAUDHARY,Minister for Parliamentary Affairs on 72-03-2O25i"This House expresses its deep gratitude to the President of Pakistan for his address toboth Houses assembled together on 10th March,2025."
MATTERS OTHER THAN POINTS OF ORDER
15. MR. SHEHRYAR AFRIDI MR. JUNAID AKBARSAHIBZADA SIBGHATULLAH MR. AMJAD AtI KHANMR. ALI MUHAMMAD to invite attention of the Minister for Energy (PowerDivision) to a matter of urgent public importance regarding loadshedding of electricity in thecountry, especially in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, causing grave concern amongst the public.
